L = dict(title='Unit 5: Project Management and Quality', points=[
 'Size metrics: productivity is KLOC per person month, plus errors per KLOC, defects per KLOC and cost per LOC',
 'Defect removal efficiency DRE equals E divided by E plus D, where E is errors before release and D is defects after release',
 'Failure percentage is failures divided by runs into 100, reliability is 100 minus failure percentage, MTBF is MTTF plus MTTR',
 'Function point: UFP is the sum of count into weight for EI, EO, EQ, ILF, EIF. VAF is 0.65 plus 0.01 into sum of Fi. FP is UFP into VAF',
 'Basic COCOMO: Effort equals a into KLOC power b, Time equals c into Effort power d. Modes are organic, semi detached, embedded',
 'Intermediate COCOMO: Effort equals a into KLOC power b into EAF, and EAF is the product of all cost drivers',
 'CPM: forward pass gives ES and EF, backward pass gives LS and LF, slack is LS minus ES, critical path has zero slack',
 'Risk exposure RE equals probability into cost. Known risks come from the plan, predictable risks from past projects, unpredictable cannot be seen in advance',
 'McCall has 11 factors in 3 groups: Product Operation 5, Product Revision 3, Product Transition 3',
 'CMM has 5 levels: Initial, Repeatable, Defined, Managed, Optimizing. Quality dilemma means aim for good enough, not perfect'], scenes=[
 S('Namaste doston! Aaj Unit five, aur yahan bhi numericals ki bharmaar hai. Socho tum Angry Birds ki tarah ek project ka launch kar rahe ho. Pehle size nikalna padega, phir kitna kaam aur kitna paisa, phir time table, phir risk, aur aakhir mein quality. Yahi is unit ka flow hai. Yeh map dhyan se dekh lo.',
  'Unit 5 map: size -> effort -> schedule -> risk -> quality',
  [['h', 'Unit 5 map'], ['row', ['Metrics LOC, FP', 'COCOMO', 'CPM, PERT']], ['row', ['SCM, QA, Monitoring', 'Risk RE = PxC', 'McCall, CMM, ISO']], ['t', 'Numericals: metrics, failure percent, FP, COCOMO, CPM, EVM, risk exposure.']],
  []),
 S('Pehle size aur quality metrics. Line of code ya LOC se hum productivity, errors per KLOC, defects per KLOC aur cost per LOC nikalte hain. Example lo. Project mein barah hazaar ek sau line of code, yaani twelve point one KLOC. Chaubees person months lage, cost ek lakh adsath hazaar, teen sau paisath page documentation, release se pehle ek sau chautees errors mile aur release ke baad unnees defects.',
  'Productivity = KLOC / PM. Quality = errors per KLOC. DRE = E / (E + D)',
  [['h', 'LOC based (size oriented) metrics'], ['tbl', [['Metric', 'Formula'], ['Productivity', 'KLOC / person-month'], ['Errors per KLOC', 'errors before release / KLOC'], ['Defects per KLOC', 'defects after release / KLOC'], ['Cost per LOC', 'total cost / LOC'], ['Pages per KLOC', 'doc pages / KLOC'], ['DRE', 'E / (E + D) x 100']]], ['t', 'Given: 12.1 KLOC, 24 PM, 168,000 cost, 365 pages, E = 134, D = 29']],
  ['## Solve', '? Productivity', '12.1 / 24 = 0.504 KLOC per PM', '? Errors per KLOC', '134 / 12.1 = 11.07', '? Defects per KLOC', '29 / 12.1 = 2.40', '? Cost per LOC', '168,000 / 12100 = 13.88', '? Pages per KLOC', '365 / 12.1 = 30.2', '! DRE = 134 / (134 + 29) = 82.2 percent']),
 S('Ab failure percentage aur reliability. Agar do sau test runs mein chhe fail hue, to failure percentage chhe divided by do sau into sau, yaani teen percent, aur reliability sattanve percent. MTTF matlab mean time to failure, MTTR matlab mean time to repair, aur MTBF barabar MTTF plus MTTR. Availability barabar MTTF divided by MTBF.',
  'Failure % = failures / runs x 100. Availability = MTTF / MTBF',
  [['h', 'Reliability terms'], ['tbl', [['Term', 'Meaning'], ['MTTF', 'Mean time to failure'], ['MTTR', 'Mean time to repair'], ['MTBF', 'MTTF + MTTR'], ['POFOD', 'Probability of failure on demand'], ['ROCOF', 'Rate of occurrence of failure'], ['Availability', 'MTTF / (MTTF + MTTR)']]], ['t', 'Trick: Bird flies MTTF hours, repair nest MTTR hours, one cycle = MTBF.']],
  ['## Failure percentage', '? 200 runs, 6 failed', 'Failure % = 6 / 200 x 100 = 3 percent', 'Reliability = 100 - 3 = 97 percent', '## MTBF and availability', '? MTTF = 200 h, MTTR = 20 h', 'MTBF = 200 + 20 = 220 h', 'Availability = 200 / 220 x 100', '! Availability = 90.9 percent']),
 S('Ab Function Points, size nikalne ka dusra tareeka jo language par depend nahi karta. Paanch cheezein gino: external inputs, external outputs, external inquiries, internal logical files aur external interface files. Har ek ka weight hota hai, simple, average, complex. Phir fourteen general system characteristics ko zero se paanch rating do, unka sum Fi. VAF barabar zero point sixty-five plus zero point zero one into sum Fi. Final FP barabar UFP into VAF.',
  'FP = UFP x VAF, VAF = 0.65 + 0.01 x sum(Fi)',
  [['h', 'Function point weights'], ['tbl', [['Component', 'Simple', 'Average', 'Complex'], ['EI inputs', '3', '4', '6'], ['EO outputs', '4', '5', '7'], ['EQ inquiries', '3', '4', '6'], ['ILF files', '7', '10', '15'], ['EIF interfaces', '5', '7', '10']]], ['t', 'Trick: 3-4-6, 4-5-7, 3-4-6, 7-10-15, 5-7-10']],
  ['## UFP (all average)', 'EI 50 x 4 = 200', 'EO 40 x 5 = 200', 'EQ 35 x 4 = 140', 'ILF 6 x 10 = 60', 'EIF 4 x 7 = 28', 'UFP = 200 + 200 + 140 + 60 + 28 = 628', '## VAF', 'Sum Fi = 46', 'VAF = 0.65 + 0.01 x 46 = 1.11', '! FP = 628 x 1.11 = 697', '? Productivity 6 FP per PM', 'Effort = 697 / 6 = 116 PM']),
 S('Ab COCOMO, end sem ka pakka numerical. Basic COCOMO mein effort barabar a into KLOC power b person months, aur time barabar c into effort power d months. Teen modes hain. Organic chhote simple projects, semi detached medium, aur embedded jahan hardware ke saath tight constraints. Coefficients ki table yaad karo. Example: organic project, battees KLOC.',
  'E = a (KLOC)^b, T = c (E)^d, Staff = E / T',
  [['h', 'Basic COCOMO coefficients'], ['tbl', [['Mode', 'a', 'b', 'c', 'd'], ['Organic', '2.4', '1.05', '2.5', '0.38'], ['Semi-detached', '3.0', '1.12', '2.5', '0.35'], ['Embedded', '3.6', '1.20', '2.5', '0.32']]], ['t', 'Trick: a goes 2.4, 3.0, 3.6 (add 0.6). b goes 1.05, 1.12, 1.20. c is always 2.5.']],
  ['## Basic COCOMO, organic 32 KLOC', 'E = 2.4 x (32)^1.05', '32^1.05 = 38.05', 'E = 2.4 x 38.05 = 91.3 PM', 'T = 2.5 x (91.3)^0.38', '91.3^0.38 = 5.56', 'T = 2.5 x 5.56 = 13.9 months', 'Staff = 91.3 / 13.9 = 6.6', '! 91.3 PM, 13.9 months, about 7 people']),
 S('Ab wahi PYQ three b. Intermediate COCOMO. Isme effort mein EAF se multiply karte hain, EAF matlab sab cost drivers ka product. Question mein size pachas hazaar line, yaani pachas KLOC. a barabar two point eight, b barabar one point two. Cost drivers: product zero point seventy-five, computer one point ten, personnel one point twenty, project zero point ninety. Pehle EAF nikalo, phir nominal effort, phir EAF se multiply.',
  'Effort = a (KLOC)^b x EAF. Pehle EAF, phir nominal, phir multiply',
  [['h', 'Intermediate COCOMO steps'], ['col', ['1. KLOC = 50000 / 1000 = 50', '2. EAF = product of all cost drivers', '3. Nominal = a x KLOC^b', '4. Effort = Nominal x EAF']], ['t', 'Marks are given step wise. Write each step.']],
  ['## PYQ 3b', 'a = 2.8, b = 1.2, size = 50 KLOC', 'EAF = 0.75 x 1.10 x 1.20 x 0.90', 'EAF = 0.891', '50^1.2 = 109.34', 'Nominal = 2.8 x 109.34 = 306.14', 'Effort = 306.14 x 0.891', '! Effort = 272.8 person months', '## Extra if asked', 'Time = 2.5 x (272.8)^0.32 = 15 months', 'Staff = 272.8 / 15 = 18 persons']),
 S('Ab project scheduling aur CPM. Scheduling matlab kaun sa kaam kab shuru aur kab khatam, Gantt chart se dikhate hain. CPM mein pehle forward pass karo, ES aur EF nikalo. Phir backward pass karo, LS aur LF. Slack barabar LS minus ES. Jinka slack zero ho wahi critical path. Yeh path late hua to poora project late. PERT mein time anuman hota hai, optimistic, most likely aur pessimistic ka weighted average. Schedule ka integration testing par bhi asar hota hai: modules late aaye to testing ka time kam, rushed integration, aur bugs bach jaate hain.',
  'Critical path = zero slack = sabse lamba raasta',
  [['h', 'Activity network (days)'], ['graph', {'A': [0.05, 0.50, 'A 3d', 'b'], 'B': [0.30, 0.15, 'B 4d', 'b'], 'C': [0.30, 0.85, 'C 2d', 'b'], 'D': [0.58, 0.15, 'D 5d', 'b'], 'E': [0.58, 0.85, 'E 3d', 'b'], 'F': [0.92, 0.50, 'F 2d', 'b']}, [['A', 'B', ''], ['A', 'C', ''], ['B', 'D', ''], ['C', 'E', ''], ['D', 'F', ''], ['E', 'F', '']], 280], ['t', 'Late module => less test time => rushed integration => escaped defects.']],
  ['## Forward pass (ES-EF)', 'A 0-3 | B 3-7 | C 3-5', 'D 7-12 | E 5-8 | F 12-14', '## Backward pass (LS-LF)', 'F 12-14 | D 7-12 | E 9-12', 'B 3-7 | C 7-9 | A 0-3', '## Slack = LS - ES', 'C = 7 - 3 = 4 | E = 9 - 5 = 4 | others 0', '! Critical path A-B-D-F = 14 days', '## PERT: O=2, M=5, P=14', 'te = (2 + 4 x 5 + 14) / 6 = 6 days', 'SD = (14 - 2) / 6 = 2']),
 S('Ab SCM, QA aur project monitoring. Software configuration management mein version control, change control, configuration audit aur status reporting aate hain. Baseline woh approved version hai jisse change sirf formal process se hota hai. Quality assurance process ko dekhta hai, quality control product ko. Monitoring ke liye earned value use karte hain. Planned value, earned value aur actual cost. SPI barabar EV divided by PV, CPI barabar EV divided by AC.',
  'SPI = EV / PV (time). CPI = EV / AC (cost). Below 1 = bura!',
  [['h', 'SCM, QA, monitoring'], ['tbl', [['Topic', 'Key points'], ['SCM', 'Baseline, version control, change control, audit, status report'], ['QA', 'Process focus: reviews, audits, standards (ISO 9001)'], ['QC', 'Product focus: testing, inspection'], ['EVM', 'PV planned, EV earned, AC actual']]]],
  ['## Earned value', '? PV = 100, EV = 80, AC = 90', 'SPI = 80 / 100 = 0.80', 'CPI = 80 / 90 = 0.89', 'SV = EV - PV = -20', 'CV = EV - AC = -10', '! Behind schedule and over budget']),
 S('Ab risk management. Teen type ke risk. Known risk woh jo project plan aur environment dekhkar pehle se pata chal jaate hain, jaise unrealistic deadline. Predictable risk woh jo pichhle projects ke experience se anuman lagate hain, jaise staff chhod ke chala jaye. Unpredictable risk ka pehle se pata nahi chalta, jaise bhukamp. Risk components chaar hain: performance, cost, support, schedule. Risk drivers woh factors hain jo in components ko prabhavit karte hain, unka impact negligible, marginal, critical ya catastrophic hota hai. Numerical: risk exposure barabar probability into cost.',
  'RE = P x C. Known = plan se, Predictable = past se, Unpredictable = surprise',
  [['h', 'Types of risk (PYQ 5a)'], ['tbl', [['Type', 'Source', 'Example'], ['Known', 'Plan, environment', 'Unrealistic deadline'], ['Predictable', 'Past projects', 'Staff turnover'], ['Unpredictable', 'Cannot foresee', 'Earthquake, new law']]], ['row', ['Performance', 'Cost', 'Support', 'Schedule']], ['t', 'Components = 4 areas. Drivers = factors with impact: negligible, marginal, critical, catastrophic.']],
  ['## Risk exposure', '? P = 0.4, cost = 50,000', 'RE = P x C = 0.4 x 50,000', '! RE = 20,000', '? Risks: 20,000 | 8,000 | 5,000', 'Total exposure = 33,000', '~ RMMM: identify, project, mitigate, monitor, manage', '~ Agile: short sprints, daily scrum, backlog reprioritising']),
 S('Ab quality dilemma. Agar tum bahut ghatiya quality ka software banaoge, to koi use khareedega nahi. Aur agar perfect banane mein itna time aur paisa lagaoge, to market nikal jayega aur paisa khatam. Isliye beech ka raasta lete hain, good enough software. Ab kya quality aur security ek hi cheez hai? Nahi. Quality bada concept hai, fit for use, jisme reliability, usability, maintainability sab aate hain. Security uska ek hissa hai, jo data ko unauthorised access se bachata hai. Ek software secure ho sakta hai par use karna mushkil, to quality kharab.',
  'Quality dilemma = beech ka raasta. Security = quality ka ek attribute',
  [['h', 'Quality dilemma (PYQ 5b)'], ['row', ['Terrible quality: nobody buys', 'Good enough: sweet spot', 'Perfect: too late, too costly']], ['tbl', [['Quality', 'Security'], ['Fit for use, many attributes', 'One attribute of quality'], ['Reliability, usability, maintainability...', 'Confidentiality, integrity, availability'], ['Whole product', 'Protection from attack']]]],
  []),
 S('Ab McCall quality model, PYQ five c. McCall ne gyarah factors teen groups mein baante. Product operation, matlab software chalte waqt kaisa hai: correctness, reliability, efficiency, integrity, usability. Product revision, matlab badalna kitna aasan: maintainability, flexibility, testability. Product transition, matlab naye jagah le jana: portability, reusability, interoperability. Paanch, teen, teen. Har factor ke neeche criteria aur metrics hote hain, aur score zero se das tak nikalte hain.',
  'McCall: 11 factors = 5 + 3 + 3 (Operation, Revision, Transition)',
  [['h', 'McCall quality model'], ['tbl', [['Group', 'Factors'], ['Product Operation (5)', 'Correctness, Reliability, Efficiency, Integrity, Usability'], ['Product Revision (3)', 'Maintainability, Flexibility, Testability'], ['Product Transition (3)', 'Portability, Reusability, Interoperability']]], ['row', ['Factors', 'Criteria', 'Metrics']], ['t', 'Trick: ORT = Operation, Revision, Transition = 5, 3, 3.']],
  ['## McCall score', '? Maintainability = c1 m1 + c2 m2 + c3 m3', 'weights 0.4, 0.3, 0.3 | scores 8, 6, 7', '= 0.4 x 8 + 0.3 x 6 + 0.3 x 7', '= 3.2 + 1.8 + 2.1', '! Score = 7.1 out of 10']),
 S('Aakhir mein CMM, capability maturity model. Yeh batata hai company ki process kitni mature hai, paanch levels. Level one Initial, sab chaos, koi process nahi. Level two Repeatable, basic project management. Level three Defined, poori company ka standard process. Level four Managed, metrics se control. Level five Optimizing, continuous improvement. Pokemon evolution ki tarah, egg se champion tak. ISO nine thousand one standard quality management system ka certificate hai. Maintenance ke chaar type: corrective, adaptive, perfective, preventive.',
  'CMM: Initial -> Repeatable -> Defined -> Managed -> Optimizing',
  [['h', 'CMM: 5 levels (Pokemon evolution)'], ['col', ['5 Optimizing: continuous improvement', '4 Managed: measured with metrics', '3 Defined: company wide standard process', '2 Repeatable: basic project management', '1 Initial: chaos, ad hoc']], ['tbl', [['Maintenance', 'Meaning'], ['Corrective', 'Fix bugs'], ['Adaptive', 'New environment'], ['Perfective', 'New features'], ['Preventive', 'Avoid future problems']]]],
  []),
])
